& [FutureLiveControlAuthorityReconsiderationGate] is the only gate by which live-control authority may be reconsidered after FSC5
  + [required_future_step] is preserve new live-control source document
  + [required_future_step] is run SJS processing into separate canonical safety authority
  + [required_future_step] is define target host inventory and resource API boundaries
  + [required_future_step] is define least-privilege credential boundary
  + [required_future_step] is define live-control dry-run and rollback proof
  + [required_future_step] is define explicit human approval, expiration, and revocation rules
  + [required_future_step] is define monitoring, abort, and fault capture routes
  + [required_future_step] is run completion review that explicitly accepts live-control scope
  + [forbidden_shortcut] is reusing FSC5 safety pack as live-control approval
  + [forbidden_shortcut] is relying on broad human approval
  + [forbidden_shortcut] is relying on dry-run success
  + [forbidden_shortcut] is relying on fixture success
  + [forbidden_shortcut] is relying on projected surface intent

  = must: require a future, separate, source-preserved, SJS-processed, least-privilege authority path for any live-control capability
  = must: keep current FSC5 work non-live after FSC5 completion

& [OperationsSafetyPackInvalidationRuleSet] is the staleness contract for FSC5OperationsSafetyPackV1
  + [invalidated_by] is change to FSC4 surface projection pack
  + [invalidated_by] is change to operations safety source
  + [invalidated_by] is change to any accepted FSC5 output hash
  + [invalidated_by] is change to any FSC5-S01 through FSC5-S06 completion review
  + [invalidated_by] is discovered contradiction among operations boundary, dry-run contract, resource safety contract, live-control prohibition, or fixture expectations
  + [invalidated_by] is any output authorizing live control without separate accepted future authority
  + [invalidated_by] is any dry-run or fixture success treated as live approval

  = must: rerun FSC5-S06 after invalidation before downstream work consumes this pack again
